For each legal perturbed game \(\mathsf G_{
u}\in\mathcal G_p\), choose a strictly positive \(\varepsilon_{
u}>0\), run \(\mathrm{def:exchange-certificate}\) until its gap is at most \(\varepsilon_{
u}\), and denote the resulting rule by \(\widetilde\delta_{
u}\). In the original experiment, on the event \(\{\widehat{\mathsf G}_n\in\mathcal G_p,\ \mathsf B_{\kappa}(\widehat{\mathsf G}_n)\}\), choose a strictly positive \(\varepsilon_n>0\), run the same construction for \(\widehat{\mathsf G}_n\) to gap at most \(\varepsilon_n\), and evaluate the certified rule at \(\widehat Z_n\); on the complementary null event set the treatment probability to \(1/2\). The resulting decision is \(\widehat\delta_n\). The sequences may converge to zero, but this construction has no zero-tolerance finite branch.
